  "linkedin": "Five DCs, added one acquisition at a time, cost €25.3M a year. Three would do the job for €2.5M less.\n\nIn this illustrative Nordic network, 33 customer cities are served from Malmö, Gothenburg, Stockholm, Oslo and Helsinki. Every DC trades kilometres against rent and stock. Fewer sites cut fixed cost and inventory, more sites cut transport, and total cost bottoms out at three: Gothenburg, Stockholm and Helsinki.\n\nThen raise transport costs 30%. The best answer moves to four DCs, and a different four: Stockholm, Oslo, Helsinki and Copenhagen. The right number of sites depends on prices you don't control.\n\nWhen did your company last check whether today's DC count is still the cheapest one?\n\nInvented numbers, real mechanics. A new planning concept every Tuesday and Thursday.\n\nFull show: The Planning Desk, supply chain news every weekday on Apple Podcasts and Spotify. Links in the first comment.\n\n#networkdesign #supplychain #logistics #nordics",
